---
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="What The Buzz Break is, who it's for, and how we cover money and tech."
>
	<section class="container prose page">
		<span class="eyebrow">About</span>
		<h1>The money and tech news that actually matters.</h1>

		<p class="lede">
			{SITE_TITLE} is an independent publication for people who want to understand the money and
			technology stories shaping their lives — without the hype, the doom, or the jargon.
		</p>

		<p>
			Every day there's a new headline about a hack, a stock, an AI launch, or a shift in the
			economy. Most coverage either assumes you already speak the language or leans on fear to win
			the click. We do the opposite: we take the one story that genuinely moved your money or your
			tech, explain it so anyone can follow, and point out the twist that most of the coverage
			skips.
		</p>

		<h2>What we promise</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Plain English.</strong> If a term needs explaining, we explain it.</li>
			<li><strong>Receipts.</strong> Every story links to the primary reporting behind it.</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Calm over clickbait.</strong> We skip words like "crash," "insane," and "you won't
				believe." The facts are interesting enough.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Explain, never advise.</strong> We help you understand what happened and what to
				watch — we never tell you what to buy, sell, or hold.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>How we report</h2>
		<p>
			We build each story from multiple established news sources and primary statements, and we're
			careful to separate what's confirmed from what's still developing. When facts are contested —
			who was behind an attack, how much was really recovered — we say so plainly and attribute the
			claim rather than stating it as settled. When a story changes, we update it and note the date.
		</p>

		<h2>Not financial advice</h2>
		<p>
			Nothing here is financial, investment, legal, or tax advice, and nothing on this site is a
			recommendation to buy or sell anything. We're a journalism and education project. For
			decisions about your own money, talk to a qualified professional who knows your situation. See
			our <a href="/disclaimer">full disclaimer</a> for the details, including how we handle affiliate
			links and advertising.
		</p>

		<h2>Say hello</h2>
		<p>
			Story tips, corrections, and partnership questions are welcome at{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. You can also follow along on YouTube,
			Instagram, TikTok, and X — all <strong>@thebuzzbreak</strong> (X: <strong
				>@thebuzzbreakhq</strong
			>).
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.page {
		padding-top: 3rem;
		padding-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.page .eyebrow {
		display: block;
	}
</style>
